# Dashboard Architecture

## Overview

The dashboard is a **project-scoped** application where users can manage multiple websites (projects). Each project is a billing unit and contains its own analytics, keywords, ICP profiles, and integrations.

## Route Structure

```
/dashboard                              → Project Hub (list all projects)
/dashboard/account                      → User account settings (NOT project-scoped)
/dashboard/projects/new                 → Create new project

/dashboard/[projectId]                  → Project Dashboard (Analytics)
/dashboard/[projectId]/settings         → Project Settings (Tabs: General, Keywords, ICP, Team, Billing)
/dashboard/[projectId]/integrations     → Integrations (Google Analytics, Search Console)
/dashboard/[projectId]/ai-copilot       → AI Copilot (future feature)
```

## Data Model

### Users & Projects Relationship

```
┌─────────────────┐
│     users       │  ← Supabase Auth user
│  id, email...   │
└────────┬────────┘
         │
         │ owns (1:n via owner_id)
         ▼
┌─────────────────┐
│    projects     │  ← Site/Website = Billing Unit
│  owner_id       │
│  name, url      │
└────────┬────────┘
         │
         │ has members (n:m)
         ▼
┌─────────────────┐
│ project_members │  ← Collaboration
│  project_id     │
│  user_id        │
│  role           │  (owner | editor | viewer)
└─────────────────┘
```

### Role Permissions

| Action | Owner | Editor | Viewer |
|--------|-------|--------|--------|
| View Dashboard | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
| Manage Keywords | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ |
| Manage ICP | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ |
| Manage Integrations | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ |
| Manage Team | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ |
| Delete Project | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ |
| Billing | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ |

## Layout Hierarchy

```
/dashboard/layout.tsx (ROOT)
├── Auth Check → Redirect to /auth/sign-in if not authenticated
├── Fetch User from DB
├── Fetch ALL projects user has access to (owned + member)
├── Provide: UserProvider + UserProjectsProvider
├── Render: Sidebar + SiteHeader + {children}
│
└── /dashboard/[projectId]/layout.tsx (NESTED)
    ├── Validate projectId from URL
    ├── Validate user has access to project
    ├── Fetch project data + user's role
    ├── Provide: ProjectProvider (current project + role)
    └── Render: {children}
```

## Providers

### Root Level (dashboard/layout.tsx)

```typescript
<DashboardProviders user={user} projects={projects}>
  // Provides:
  // - UserProvider: { user, isLoading }
  // - UserProjectsProvider: { projects: ProjectWithRole[], isLoading }
</DashboardProviders>
```

### Project Level ([projectId]/layout.tsx)

```typescript
<ProjectProvider project={project} role={role}>
  // Provides:
  // - project: Project (current project)
  // - role: 'owner' | 'editor' | 'viewer'
  // - isLoading: boolean
</ProjectProvider>
```

## Sidebar Navigation

The sidebar dynamically changes based on context:

### When NOT in a project (/dashboard, /dashboard/account)

```typescript
navMain = [
  { title: "Projects", url: "/dashboard", icon: IconFolder }
]
```

### When IN a project (/dashboard/[projectId]/*)

```typescript
navMain = [
  { title: "Overview", url: `/dashboard/${projectId}` },
  { title: "AI Copilot", url: `/dashboard/${projectId}/ai-copilot` },
  { title: "Project Settings", url: `/dashboard/${projectId}/settings` },
  { title: "Integrations", url: `/dashboard/${projectId}/integrations` },
]
```

## Key Services

### project-service.ts

```typescript
// Get all projects user has access to
getUserProjects(userId: string): Promise<ProjectWithRole[]>

// Get specific project with user's role (for access validation)
getProjectWithRole(projectId: string, userId: string): Promise<ProjectWithRole | null>

// Get project by ID (no access check)
getProjectById(projectId: string): Promise<Project | null>
```

### project-members.service.ts

```typescript
// Collaboration
inviteMember(projectId, { email, role })
acceptInvitation(userId, userEmail, { token })
getProjectMembers(projectId)
getUserProjectRole(projectId, userId)
updateMemberRole({ projectId, userId, role })
removeMember(projectId, userId)
```

## Project Switcher Behavior

1. Shows current project name + role badge
2. Dropdown lists ALL projects user has access to
3. Clicking a project navigates to `/dashboard/[newProjectId]`
4. **Preserves sub-path**: If on `/dashboard/abc/settings`, switching to project XYZ goes to `/dashboard/xyz/settings`

## Settings Page Tabs

Located at `/dashboard/[projectId]/settings`:

| Tab | Content | Access |
|-----|---------|--------|
| **General** | Project name, URL, delete project | Owner only for edit |
| **Keywords** | `KeywordsManager` component | Owner, Editor |
| **ICP** | `IcpManager` component | Owner, Editor |
| **Team** | `MembersTab` - invite, manage roles | Owner only |
| **Billing** | Stripe integration (coming soon) | Owner only |

## Pricing Model

- **Per-site billing**: Each project is a billing unit
- **Owner pays**: The project owner is responsible for the subscription
- **Flexible for agencies**: One user can own multiple projects, each billed separately

## Authentication Flow

```
1. User visits /dashboard
2. middleware.ts checks Supabase session
   → No session? Redirect to /auth/sign-in
3. dashboard/layout.tsx fetches user + projects
   → No user in DB? Redirect to /auth/sign-in
4. dashboard/page.tsx (Project Hub)
   → 0 projects? Redirect to /auth/onboarding
   → 1 project? Redirect to /dashboard/[projectId]
   → 2+ projects? Show project selection grid
```

